  ],
  "details": "<p>The name of the <em>tribus Papiria</em> derives from the Roman <em>gens Papiria</em>. The tribe presumably was located in the territory of Labicum (or Labici) and in the fourth century B.C. Tusculum was enfranchised in this tribe.</p>",
  "review_state": "published",
  "type": "FeatureCollection",
  "description": "The tribus Papiria is one of the earliest rural tribes of Rome.",
